PVD("brunei_ndp_2012-2017",{"docs":["","BRU NDP 2012 2017"],"s":{"1":[[1,"16","5","Programme Monitoring and Periodic Project Evaluation Mechanism","Several reforms have also been introduced by the Executive Committee for RKN10 to ensure transparency and accountability, especially in terms of more objective programme monitoring, including mechanisms for scheduled periodic project evaluations, in order to ensure that RKN10's implementation focus will be of a higher quality and will meet the targeted timelines that have been set.",""],[1,"16","6","Site Visit-Based Project Monitoring and Remedial Action","I intend to personally conduct site visits to specific project sites to ensure progress in their implementation, whilst at the same time staying informed of the latest project developments.",""],[1,"51","4","Infrastructure Contract Award and Management Review","Reviewing the way government infrastructure contracts are awarded and managed in order to ensure that these infrastructure are implemented on time and cost effectively.",""],[1,"70","10","Ministry-Level Consultant Appointment Committees","Establishing a committee for the appointment of consultants in every ministry to expedite the appointment process, which previously existed only within the Ministry of Development;",""],[1,"70","11","Variation Orders Approval Procedure Reform","Changing the procedure for Variation Orders approval;",""],[1,"70","15","Strengthen In-House Technical Capacity for Project Implementation","Enhancing ministries' and departments' capacity in implementing projects by engaging more in-house technical staff to reduce dependency on the Ministry of Development;",""],[1,"70","16","Programme and Project Monitoring Effectiveness Improvement","Improving the effectiveness of processes involved in monitoring programmes and projects.",""],[1,"72","1","Organised and Effective Monitoring System","These positive developments will be further enhanced during the RKN10 period through the use of alternative implementation methods as well as by an organised and effective monitoring system, in an effort to accomplish the country's development objectives.",""],[1,"136","8","RKN10 Project Monitoring Committee","the appointment of the RKN10 Working Committee will be maintained throughout the duration of RKN10 with the purpose of monitoring the projects.",""],[1,"136","8","Ministry Project Performance Monitoring Using KPIs","Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) will be used to monitor the performance of the ministries in carrying out their respective projects.",""],[1,"136","8","Scheduled Project Site Visits","The committee will also be involved in making scheduled visits to project sites.",""],[1,"136","10","Project Implementation and Removal Review Mechanism","All projects must be implemented within the first year of RKN10.",""]],"2":[[1,"16","4","Re-evaluation of Programme and Project Funding Allocation","the re-evaluation of the allocation of funding for programmes and projects that have been considered will next take into account the programmes and projects that are characterised by effectiveness in terms of cost, value for money, project priority and the significance to the nation, as well as mutually complementing the essence and goals of RKN10 including its readiness for implementation.",""],[1,"30","4","Project Selection and Budget Allocation Reform","a new approach for the selection of projects and budget allocation has been adopted, which is based on the following three principles: i) Prudent spending; ii) Project priority; and iii) Avoidance of wastage",""],[1,"51","3","Funding Assurance for Priority Government Infrastructure Projects","Ensuring that funding is available for all priority government infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"70","12","Reduction of Bankers' Guarantee Rates","Reducing bankers' guarantee rates to ease the contractor's financial burden;",""],[1,"71","1","Continuation of Incomplete Projects Under RKN10","the government has carried forward incomplete projects to be implemented during the RKN10 period with an allocation of BND3,769.2 million.",""],[1,"71","1","Selection of Ready-for-Implementation Projects","only projects which are ready for implementation will be carried forward.",""],[1,"72","1","Alternative Implementation Methods for Development Projects","These positive developments will be further enhanced during the RKN10 period through the use of alternative implementation methods as well as by an organised and effective monitoring system, in an effort to accomplish the country's development objectives.",""]],"3":[[1,"118","4","Public Sector ICT Infrastructure Provision","The government will continue to provide the necessary infrastructure in accordance with current needs.",""],[1,"118","5","Digital Government Online Services Initiative","One of the initiatives being implemented is the provision of online services such as e-Darussalam, e-Payment, e-Postcode, Online Business Registration, Online Business Licensing System, Government Employees Management System (GEMS), Treasury Accounting and Financial Information System (TAFIS), iLearn and e-Custom.",""],[1,"126","3","E-Government Service Integration Initiative","Within the RKN10 period, the government will continue to implement the e-government initiatives in order to facilitate and expedite dealings between the public and the government.",""],[1,"168","13","Hydrocarbon Data Management Information System Phase II Development Programme","Hydrocarbon Data Management Information System (HDMIS) - Phase II Development Programme for Science and Technology Quality Management System (PBD ISO 9001-2000)",""],[1,"168","20","PMO Data Centre Capacity and Services Expansion","Expansion and Enhancement of PMO'S Data Centre Capacity and Services",""],[1,"168","20","DEFLIS Enhancement","DEFLIS Enhancement",""],[1,"168","20","Multimedia Development Commissioning","Multimedia Development Commissioning of the Planning Information Databank (Phase II)",""],[1,"168","21","PMONet Infrastructure Expansion Phase II","Expansion of PMONet Infrastructure for the Royal Brunei Police Force - Phase II 1.28",""],[1,"168","16","Public Key Infrastructure Provision","Provision of Public Key Infrastructure (PKI)",""],[1,"169","13","Disaster Recovery Centre at E-Government National Centre","Disaster Recovery Centre at E-Government National Centre with Hardware, Software and Related Accessories",""],[1,"169","14","e-Consular System for Missions Abroad","e-Consular System with Hardware, Software and Related Accessories for Missions Abroad",""],[1,"169","10","Facilities Management System Implementation","Implementation of Facilities Management System for Department of Planning and Estate Management, Ministry of Education","Ministry of Education"],[1,"169","1","Spatial Data Infrastructure Establishment","Establishment of Spatial Data Infrastructure",""]],"4":[[1,"9","5","Education and Skills Development Across Priority Sectors","emphasis must be given to the effective provision of education and the development of skills in all areas such as science and technology, engineering, security, economy, business, entrepreneurship, health and agri-food, while not neglecting such areas as society, culture, religion and the environment.",""],[1,"47","2","Early Childhood Education Investment","1. Investing in early childhood education.",""],[1,"47","4","Secondary and Tertiary Education Expansion","Providing high standards of secondary and tertiary education, including vocational schools, which will produce experts, professionals and technicians required in commerce and industry.",""],[1,"47","5","ICT Competency and Curriculum Integration in Schools","Strengthening competency in info-communications technology (ICT) among students, teachers and educational administrators, including the integration of ICT in the school curriculum.",""],[1,"47","6","Lifelong Learning and Higher Education Access Programme","Devising programmes that promote life-long learning and widen access to higher education.",""],[1,"47","8","Technology-Enabled Cost-Effective Education","Adopting cost-effective methods of educating our people through the use of technology.",""],[1,"89","3","EduCare Early Childhood Education Project","the implementation of the EduCare Project which aims to provide all children with equal opportunit.",""],[1,"92","4","Strengthening the Learning Environment for STI and Innovative Thinking","the learning environment fostered through SPN21 will provide opportunities for young students to showcase innovative thinking through stimulating ideas and discussions.",""],[1,"92","4","Expanded Secondary Computer Science Curriculum","Computer Science will also be given more emphasis as one of the subjects at the secondary level, specifically to support the Science, Technology, Environment Partnership (STEP) initiative under the Ministry of Education.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"93","3","Education and Skills Development Policies","The government will continue its efforts to implement policies that can create a well-educated and highly skilled population, which is key to the development of a sustainable economy.",""],[1,"93","5","Learning Facilities and Research-Based Productivity Programme","New approaches and programmes need to be explored and prepared, not only by the government but also through close collaboration with, and with integrated efforts from, various agencies to provide learning facilities, the use of research activities and technological advances in generating high and sustainable productivity as well as an economy that is based on knowledge.",""]],"5":[[1,"168","15","e-Services Infrastructure Phase II Technology Refresh for Secondary Schools","e-Services Infrastructure Phase II - Technology Refresh for all Secondary Schools",""],[1,"168","16","e-Services Infrastructure Phase II Technology Refresh for Primary Schools","e-Services Infrastructure Phase II - Technology Refresh for all Primary Schools",""],[1,"168","16","ICT Competency Programme","ICT Competency Programme",""],[1,"169","1","ICT Hardware and Peripherals for Ministry of Education","ICT Hardware and Peripherals for Ministry of Education New Headquarter Office","Ministry of Education"],[1,"169","1","ICT Hardware and Peripherals for New Schools","ICT Hardware and Peripherals for New Primary and Secondary Schools (Administration and Libraries)",""]],"6":[[1,"29","5","Education Infrastructure and Facilities Improvement","Quality education infrastructure and facilities;",""],[1,"88","4","Quality Education Infrastructure Development","RKN10 will emphasise on the development of quality education infrastructure and the provision of facilities that will foster a conducive, stimulating and effective learning and teaching environment.",""],[1,"89","1","Education Infrastructure and Facilities Improvement Programme","The government will provide more infrastructure and facilities for education by constructing, upgrading, improving and maintaining school buildings and educational institutions, as well as supplying furniture, equipments and other facilities.",""],[1,"89","2","Disability Support Facilities for Education Access","facilities such as hostels and transportation will continue to be provided to ensure that they can duly receive adequate education in a similarly conducive learning environment.",""],[1,"92","7","Private Sector Capacity Expansion for Student Accommodation","The private sector is encouraged to give their utmost support through increasing their capacity to accommodate the rising number of students every year.",""],[1,"161","8","School Building Construction and Upgrading Programme","New Building for Mulaut Primary School Building for Kampong Sungai Akar and Kampong Lumut Belait Secondary School Brunei Institute of Technology - Phase III Preliminary Works for Higher Education Institute External Infrastructure Works of Meragang Secondary School Site ICT Lab for Universiti Brunei Darussalam Jefri Bolkiah College of Engineering, Kuala Belait - Phase I Sultan Saiful Rijal Technical College - Phase I Rebuilding of Pintu Malim Primary School Building Rebuilding of Temporary School Buildings and Schools in Kampong Ayer - Phase I Rebuilding of Paduka Seri Begawan Sultan Science College Jalan Muara Upgrading of Primary Schools Building and Infrastructure Phase I Upgrading of School Building and Ministry of Education Housing throughout the Country",""],[1,"162","1","Upgrading and Renovation of Sport Facilities in Educational Institutions","Upgrading and Renovation of Sport Facilities for Secondary Schools, Colleges and Vocational Institutes throughout the Country",""],[1,"162","2","Primary School Upgrading Programme","Upgrading of Primary Schools - Orang Kaya Setia Bakti Kilanas; Tanah Jambu; Sultan Abdul Bubin, Sungai Besar; Sultan Umar Ali Saifuddien, Muara; Bengkurong; and Pengkalan Batu",""],[1,"162","3","Sultan Saiful Rijal Technical College Phase II Construction and Upgrading","Construction and Upgrading of Sultan Saiful Rijal Technical College - Phase II",""],[1,"162","3","Mechanical Training Centre Phase II Construction and Upgrading","Construction and Upgrading of Mechanical Training Centre - Phase II",""],[1,"162","3","Secondary Schools, Colleges and Sixth Form Centres Construction and Upgrading","Construction and Upgrading of Secondary Schools, Colleges and Sixth Form Centres",""],[1,"162","3","Katok B Primary School Phase II Construction and Upgrading","Construction and Upgrading of Katok 'B' Primary School - Phase II",""],[1,"162","4","Perpindahan Rimba III Primary School Construction and Upgrading Phase II","Construction and Upgrading of Perpindahan Rimba III Primary School - Phase II",""],[1,"162","4","PSB SOAS Belait Primary School Construction and Upgrading Phase II","Construction and Upgrading of PSB SOAS Belait Primary School - Phase II",""],[1,"162","5","Construction and Upgrading of Sultan Sharif Ali Islamic University","Construction and Upgrading of Sultan Sharif Ali Islamic University",""],[1,"162","5","Construction of Hall, Chancellor's Office and Computer Centre for ITB","Construction of Hall, Chancellor's Office and Computer Centre for ITB",""],[1,"162","5","Construction of Seri Begawan Religious Teachers University College","Construction of Seri Begawan Religious Teachers University College",""],[1,"162","6","Construction of Arabic Secondary School Kampong Katok","Construction of Arabic Secondary School Kampong Katok",""],[1,"162","7","Construction of Rataie Secondary School","Construction of Rataie Secondary School, Temburong",""],[1,"162","8","Construction of Kampong Bolkiah Religious School","Construction of Kampong Bolkiah Religious School",""],[1,"162","9","Construction of Religious School for Mentiri National Housing Scheme","Construction of Religious School for Mentiri National Housing Scheme",""],[1,"162","12","Laboratory Infrastructure Network II for New Secondary Schools","Laboratory Infrastructure Network II for New Secondary Schools",""],[1,"162","13","Laboratory Infrastructure Network II for New Primary Schools","Laboratory Infrastructure Network II for New Primary Schools",""]],"7":[[1,"90","6","Technical and Vocational Education Scholarship Scheme","The introduction of the Technical and Vocational Education Scholarship Scheme (BPTV) at the local private institutions on 15th July 2011 provides opportunities for local school leavers who have completed their 'O' and 'A' levels or its equivalent to pursue higher education.",""],[1,"10","1","Workforce Continuous Training Programme","Every member of the workforce must be provided with on-going and appropriate training to keep them abreast of the latest technological developments to assist them in their jobs.",""],[1,"29","5","Professional and Highly Skilled Workforce Development","Professional and highly skilled workforce;",""],[1,"48","9","Commerce and Industry Skills Development through Education and R&D Investment","Developing the expertise and skills required by commerce and industry through investment in our educational institutions, in research and development, and through collaborations with businesses.",""],[1,"61","4","Local Labour Force Employability Enhancement Schemes","Other efforts are also being implemented such as enhancing the employability of the local labour force through various education and training schemes.",""],[1,"63","6","Human Resource Development Capacity Building","The government through relevant agencies will focus on efforts to promote the following: innovation and the use of advanced technology; capacity building through investments in human resource development; research activities which can be commercialised; and streamlining processes to better facilitate the start-up of businesses and investments in the country.",""],[1,"68","1","Human Resource Development Fund","and the Human Resource Development Fund.",""],[1,"90","5","Workforce Retraining and Skills Enhancement Programmes","The provision of retraining and delivery of skills among the work force will further be reinforced",""],[1,"90","7","Private Sector Human Capacity Building Scheme","the Human Capacity Building Scheme in the Private Sector (PSTS) has been introduced to enable them to upgrade their academic qualifications and improve their professionalism so that they become more capable and more competitive in the labour market.",""],[1,"90","7","Training and Employment Scheme","through the Training and Employment Scheme (SLP), local school leavers will be given skills training and work experiences in various fields to enable them to enter the labour market more easily.",""],[1,"90","8","In-Service Training for Public Sector Employees","programmes under the In-Service Training for the public sector employees will also continue to be made available to ensure improvements in the quality of its workforce.",""],[1,"91","1","Lifelong Learning and Skills Upgrading Initiative","efforts to encourage the local population, particularly those in the labour force, to continue acquiring knowledge and upgrading their skills will be implemented to ensure a continuous increase in productivity, either in the public or private sectors.",""],[1,"91","2","Special Classes for Continuing Education","improving and increasing the provision of special classes for continuing education.",""],[1,"91","2","Skills Courses Expansion","Skills courses will also continue to be provided and expanded by various ministries and private institutions in order to produce competitive students and workforce, as well as to increase opportunities for employment.",""],[1,"97","1","Youth Skills Development Training Courses","various training courses for skills development will continue to be provided.",""]],"8":[[1,"137","10","Human Resource Development Fund","A total of BND250 million has been allocated under the Human Resource Development Fund for the development of human resources.",""]],"9":[[1,"99","7","Forest Rehabilitation and Corrective Measures","Brunei Darussalam will continue to preserve its status as a country with the world's most extensively protected tropical rainforest by ensuring that corrective measures and rehabilitation of forests will continue to be implemented.",""],[1,"158","7","Inventory and Silvicultural Improvement of Natural Forest Products","Inventory and Silvicultural Improvement of Natural Forest Products",""],[1,"158","8","Forestry Patrol Road Construction","Forestry Patrol Road to Control and Monitor Transborder Forest",""],[1,"158","8","Selirong Island Forest Recreation Park Public Facilities Upgrade","Upgrading of Public Facilities at Selirong Island Forest Recreation Park Stage 2",""],[1,"158","8","Forest Recreational Parks Public Facilities Upgrade","Upgrading of Public Facilities in Forest Recreational Parks Stage 3",""],[1,"158","8","Forest Recreational Parks Development and Upgrading","Development and Upgrading of Forest Recreational Parks Stage 2",""],[1,"159","1","Sawn Timber Plantation Development, Stage 2","Development of Sawn Timber Plantations, Stage 2",""],[1,"159","1","Rattan Development Programme","Rattan Development",""],[1,"159","1","Tropical Forest Biodiversity Centre Construction","Construction of Tropical Forest Biodiversity Centre",""],[1,"159","1","Forest Production Inspection Station Construction, Phase II","Construction of Inspection Station for Forest Production - Phase II",""],[1,"159","1","Wasteland Rehabilitation, Stage 3","Rehabilitation of Wasteland Stage 3",""],[1,"159","1","Eco-Tourism Site Master Planning","Master Plan for Eco-Tourism Sites",""],[1,"159","1","Forest Resources Management Programme","Development and Management of Forest Resources Programme",""],[1,"159","1","Forest Road Network Development, Stage 2","Forest Road Network Stage 2",""],[1,"159","1","Forest Production Control and Inspection Station","Control and Inspection Station for Forest Production",""]],"10":[[1,"51","9","Environmental Standards Compliance for Industry","Implementing the best environmental standards for existing and new industries in Brunei Darussalam in accordance with established international standards and practices.",""],[1,"51","11","Environmental Health and Safety Regulation Enforcement","Enforcing strictly appropriate regulations regarding the environment that affect public health and safety.",""],[1,"51","12","Support for Global and Regional Environmental Cooperation","Supporting global and regional efforts to address trans-border and regional environmental concerns.",""]],"11":[[1,"100","2","Disaster Risk Protection and Public Safety Measures","the government through the relevant agencies will intensify efforts to safeguard and protect its people from any threat and natural disasters such as landslides, floods and others.",""],[1,"101","4","Disaster Risk Protection and Public Safety Measures","the government through the relevant agencies will intensify efforts to safeguard and protect its people from any threat and natural disasters such as landslides, floods and others.",""],[1,"100","3","National Disaster Management Centre","the establishment of the National Disaster Management Centre (NDMC) which has the responsibility in taking prompt and effective actions against any disasters",""],[1,"100","3","Weather Forecasting and Radar Technology Upgrade","the installation of a sophisticated weather forecasting system and radar resolution technology, which are expected to be completed in 2012 and which will enhance the capacity of weather monitoring and warning dissemination",""]],"12":[[1,"98","6","Health Facility Infrastructure Upgrading and Expansion","the government will continue to upgrade the infrastructure and facilities at existing hospitals and clinics.",""],[1,"98","6","New Health Infrastructure Construction Programme","the construction and provision of new infrastructure and facilities will be implemented to fulfil current and immediate needs.",""],[1,"162","23","National Medical and Health Store New Hospital for Women and Children (Phase I)","National Medical and Health Store New Hospital for Women and Children (Phase I)",""],[1,"162","25","Hospital Upgrading and Health Equipment Replacement","Upgrading of Hospital and Replacement of Health Equipments",""],[1,"162","26","Pengiran Isteri Hajah Mariam Hospital Upgrading","Upgrading of Pengiran Isteri Hajah Mariam Hospital",""],[1,"162","27","RIPAS Hospital Wards and Facilities Upgrade Phase II","Upgrading of Wards and Facilities at Raja Isteri Pengiran Anak Saleha (RIPAS) Hospital Phase II",""],[1,"162","28","Ministry of Health Master Plan","Ministry of Health Master Plan","Ministry of Health"],[1,"162","28","Equipment for New Women and Children Hospital","Equipment for New Women and Children Hospital",""],[1,"162","28","Phase I Renovation Project for Building Upgrade","Phase I Renovation Project for Building Upgrade",""],[1,"162","28","Dialysis Centre Tutong","Dialysis Centre Tutong",""],[1,"163","1","Sultan Omar Ali Saifuddien Health Centre","Sultan Omar Ali Saifuddien (SOAS) Kg Sungai Kebun Health Centre",""],[1,"163","1","Dental Centre","Dental Centre",""],[1,"163","1","New Children Development Centre","New Children Development Centre for National Tuberculosis Programme",""],[1,"163","1","Medical Transfusion Centre","Medical Transfusion Centre",""],[1,"163","1","Ward and Facilities Upgrade at RIPAS Hospital","Ward and Facilities at RIPAS Hospital",""],[1,"163","1","Ward and Facilities Upgrade at Suri Seri Begawan Hospital","Ward and Facilities at Suri Seri Begawan, Kuala Belait Hospital - Phase IV",""]],"13":[[1,"97","4","National Housing Schemes","Various national housing schemes will continue to be implemented in order to fulfill the increasing demand for houses and to provide adequate housing.",""],[1,"97","5","Sustainable Housing Construction Subsidy Support","In addition to expediting the construction of houses, emphasis will also be given to sustainable and optimal methods of construction, in terms of land utilisation, costs and the provision of government subsidies.",""],[1,"97","6","Vertical Housing Priority Policy","the government will give priority to houses built using the vertical housing concept.",""],[1,"164","3","National Housing and Resettlement Schemes","Infrastructure and General Housing Works Kampong Bukit Beruang, Tutong National Housing Kampong Keriam, Tutong National Housing Kampong Keriam, Tutong National Housing Kampong Lambak Kanan, Brunei Muara National Housing Kampong Lorong Tengah Seria, Belait National Housing Kampong Lugu National Housing - Phase I Kampong Lugu National Housing - Extension Kampong Lumut/Sungai Liang, Belait National Housing Kampong Meragang, Brunei Muara National Housing Kampong Pandan, Belait National Housing Kampong Rataie, Temburong National Housing Kampong Tanah Jambu, Brunei Muara National Housing Mengkubau, Brunei Muara National Housing Kampong Ayer Resettlement Scheme at Kampong Katok 'B' Kampong Ayer Resettlement Scheme at Kampong Lumapas 'A' Resettlement and Housing Scheme, Kampong Rimba Kampong Sungai Buloh/Tanah Jambu Kanan Landless Indigenous Citizen Housing Scheme",""]],"14":[[1,"163","2","Kampong Ukong Mosque Construction","Construction of Kampong Ukong Mosque Construction of Lumut I Mosque",""],[1,"163","2","Lumut I Mosque Construction","Construction of Kampong Ukong Mosque Construction of Lumut I Mosque",""],[1,"163","3","Construction of Mosques in Multiple Locations","Construction of Mosques at Kampong Madang/Manggis, Mulaut, Sungai Akar, Batong and Tungku/Katok",""],[1,"163","3","Provision of Prayer Areas in Religious Schools","Provision of Prayer Areas in Religious Schools",""],[1,"163","3","Religious School Extension at Mentiri National Housing Scheme","Mentiri National Housing Scheme Religious School Extension to Kampong Keriam Mosque",""],[1,"163","3","Mosque and School Asset and Infrastructure Upgrading Programme","U.S.A.I. (Upgrading and Sustaining of Asset and Infrastructure) - Mosques and Schools",""],[1,"167","5","Extension of the Ministry of Religious Affairs Building at Labu Immigration Checkpoint","Extension to Ministry of Religious Affairs Building Labu Immigration Checkpoint, Labu, Temburong","Ministry of Religious Affairs"]],"16":[[1,"48","6","World-Class Infrastructure Investment for Export Industries","Investing in world class infrastructure necessary to attract foreign and domestic investments in new export industries.",""],[1,"49","8","Special Economic Zone Regulatory Frameworks","Introducing regulatory frameworks in line with international best practices, such as those applicable to special economic zones to facilitate competitiveness in promoting foreign direct investments.",""],[1,"68","2","Industrial Development and Sungai Liang Industrial Park Project","which included significant industrial development and the Sungai Liang Industrial Park project.",""],[1,"114","3","Industrial Cluster Development Initiative","the government has identified several industrial clusters.",""],[1,"115","1","Non-Oil Industrial Development Strategy","a non-oil industrial development strategy will be implemented to widen opportunities for local SMEs.",""],[1,"127","3","Industrial Site Development under RKN10","more industrial sites will be established under the RKN10 to facilitate and expand industrial activities.",""],[1,"127","4","Development of Industrial and Export Industry Sites","Among the sites that have been identified for development include the Sungai Liang Industrial Park, Pulau Muara Besar, Kampung Telisai, and the Kampong Tanah Jambu Industrial Site.",""],[1,"127","4","Provision of High-Quality Infrastructure for Industrial Sites","These sites will eventually be provided with high-quality infrastructure.",""],[1,"159","14","Kuala Lurah Industrial Site Infrastructure Upgrade","Upgrading of Kuala Lurah Industrial Site Infrastructure and Facilities",""],[1,"159","14","Serambangun Industrial Site Infrastructure Upgrade","Upgrading of Serambangun, Tutong Industrial Site Infrastructure and Facilities",""],[1,"159","14","Aquaculture Industrial Site Basic Infrastructure Provision","Providing Additional Basic Infrastructure for Aquaculture Industrial Site Development",""],[1,"159","14","Industrial Site Development and Tourism Promotion","Industrial Site Development and Promotion of Tourism Sector",""],[1,"159","16","Pulau Muara Besar Phase II Development","Development of Pulau Muara Besar - Phase II Development of Lambak Kanan East Industrial Site Development of Brunei Bay (Pulau Muara Besar) Construction of Sg Liang Jetty Incubation and Primary Resource Excellence Management Increasing Compliance to International Standards by Local SMEs Provision of Tourism Industry Facilities",""],[1,"159","16","Lambak Kanan East Industrial Site Development","Development of Pulau Muara Besar - Phase II Development of Lambak Kanan East Industrial Site Development of Brunei Bay (Pulau Muara Besar) Construction of Sg Liang Jetty Incubation and Primary Resource Excellence Management Increasing Compliance to International Standards by Local SMEs Provision of Tourism Industry Facilities",""],[1,"159","16","Brunei Bay Development at Pulau Muara Besar","Development of Pulau Muara Besar - Phase II Development of Lambak Kanan East Industrial Site Development of Brunei Bay (Pulau Muara Besar) Construction of Sg Liang Jetty Incubation and Primary Resource Excellence Management Increasing Compliance to International Standards by Local SMEs Provision of Tourism Industry Facilities",""],[1,"160","1","Development of Enterprise Sites","Development of Enterprise Sites",""],[1,"160","1","Development of New Industrial Sites","Development of New Industrial Sites",""],[1,"160","1","Lambak Industrial Site","Lambak Industrial Site",""],[1,"160","1","Serasa Industrial Area","Serasa Industrial Area",""],[1,"160","1","ABC Sungai Liang Industrial Site","ABC Sungai Liang Industrial Site",""]],"17":[[1,"158","3","Post-Harvest Technological Development Phase II Poultry Development","Post-harvest Technological Development Phase II Poultry Technological Development - Kampongs' Poultry Farming (Breeding, Egg and Meat)",""],[1,"158","6","Agricultural Support Schemes","Agricultural Support Schemes Development Scheme for Broiler Chicken Industry - Phase II Development Scheme for Cluster Agricultural Plantation Development Scheme for Agricultural Research and Development Development of Agricultural BioTechnology and Agri-Food Development Scheme for Paddy Production",""]],"19":[[1,"124","4","Water Supply Disruption, Flash Flood and Pollution Control","The disruption of water supply, flash floods and environmental pollution that have impaired social and economic activities and caused property damage and loss of life will continue to be addressed and controlled.",""],[1,"165","6","Sewerage Treatment Plant Improvement","Improvement of Sewerage Treatment Plant Improvement of Sewerage Treatment Plants",""],[1,"166","6","Temburong River Cleaning and Deepening","Cleaning and Deepening of Temburong River",""],[1,"166","6","Concrete Drain Construction at Kampong Tanjong Bunut","Construction of Concrete Drains at Kampong Tanjong Bunut Area",""],[1,"166","6","Concrete Drain Construction at Kampong Sungai Tilong and Kampong Salambigar","Construction of Concrete Drains at Kampong Sungai Tilong and Kampong Salambigar Areas, Jalan Muara",""],[1,"166","6","Town Centre Drainage System Upgrading","Upgrading of Drainage System at Town Centre, Bandar Seri Begawan",""],[1,"166","6","Sungai Bebuhun Drainage System Upgrading","Upgrading of Drainage System at Sungai Bebuhun",""],[1,"166","6","Mukim Lumut and Belait Drainage System Upgrading","Upgrading of Drainage System at Mukim Lumut and Belait",""],[1,"166","8","Drainage Improvement at Kampong Lumapas Phase II","Drainage Improvement at Kampong Lumapas Phase II",""],[1,"166","8","Drainage Improvement at Sungaia Belaban, Kampong Tungku Phase II","Drainage Improvement at Sungaia Belaban, Kampong Tungku - Phase II",""],[1,"166","8","Drainage Improvement at Sungai Damuan, Kampong Lugu Housing Scheme","Drainage Improvement at Sungai Damuan (Kampong Lugu Housing Scheme)",""],[1,"166","10","Drainage Improvement at Pekan Tutong Phase II","Drainage Improvement at Pekan Tutong - Phase II",""],[1,"166","10","Drainage Structure Improvement Towards Sea at Belait River","Improvement of Drainage Structure towards Sea at Belait River",""],[1,"166","10","Concrete Drain and Retaining Pond Construction in Damuan Catchment","Construction of Concrete Drains and Retaining Ponds - Damuan Catchment",""],[1,"166","11","Kampong Ban/Mulaut Flood Alleviation Project Phase II","Kampong Ban/Mulaut Flood Alleviation Project Phase II",""],[1,"166","11","Flood Mitigation Scheme at Pekan Seria, Belait District - Phase II","Flood Mitigation Scheme at Pekan Seria, Belait District - Phase II",""],[1,"166","11","Subok-Belimbing Flood Mitigation Scheme Phase IV","Subok - Belimbing Flood Mitigation Scheme Phase IV",""],[1,"166","12","Kampong Belimbing and Subok Catchment Flood Mitigation Scheme - Stage 3","Kampong Belimbing and Subok Catchment Flood Mitigation Scheme - Stage 3",""],[1,"166","13","Temburong Flood Mitigation Scheme Phase II","Temburong Flood Mitigation Scheme - Phase II",""],[1,"166","14","Flood Mitigation Scheme at Tutong River","Flood Mitigation Scheme at Tutong River",""],[1,"168","3","Flood Prevention Feasibility Study","Feasibility Study on Flood Prevention throughout the Country",""]],"21":[[1,"101","5","Water Supply Capacity and Conservation Measures","the government will continue to implement various efforts to ensure the level and quality of the water supply is sufficient to meet demands of national development, particularly with the increasing population and industrial development.",""],[1,"124","3","Clean Water Supply and Sewerage Infrastructure Improvement","The government will continue to be responsible for the supply and distribution of clean water and for the improvement of the drainage and sewerage systems.",""],[1,"124","3","Use of High-Quality Materials and New Technology for Water Infrastructure","the government will make certain the use of high quality materials and new technology which will also help to reduce expenditure on assets' maintenance costs.",""],[1,"165","13","Belait Water Supply Source Improvement Works","Source Improvement Works for Belait Water Supply - Kargu Dam",""],[1,"165","13","Brunei Muara and Tutong Water Supply Source Improvement Works","Source Improvement Works for Brunei Muara and Tutong Water Supply - Ulu Tutong Dam",""],[1,"165","14","Main Water Pipe Supply and Installation Project","Supply and Installation of New Main Water Pipes from Bukit Barun to Brunei Muara (along Tutong-Brunei Muara Highway)",""],[1,"165","15","Screening Technology Supply and Installation at Bukit Barun Water Treatment Plant","Supply and Installation of Screening Technology at Bukit Barun Water Treatment Plant",""],[1,"166","1","National Water Supply and Treatment Infrastructure Upgrades","Supply and Replacement of Water Pipes throughout the Country Construction of Water Treatment Plant, Raw Water Pump Station, Water Reservoir and Clean Water - Bukit Barun Stage 7 Enhancement of Services Control Centre for Brunei Muara, Tutong, Kuala Belait and Temburong Improvement of Water Storage Capacity for Mengkubau Dam Improvement of Water Treatment Plants throughout the Country Improvement of Water Resource for Belait District Water Supply - Ulu Belait Dam Construction of Additional Water Treatment Plant Sungai Liang Construction of New Water Reservoir Terminal Construction of Water Reservoirs throughout the Country Survey Mapping for Water Catchment Area and New Works Planned Maintenance System Tambahan Mengkubau Water Treatment Plant Temburong Riverfront",""],[1,"169","1","Water Supply Management System","Water Supply Management System",""],[1,"169","1","Water Pipe Network Management System for Kuala Belait","Water Pipe Network Management System - Kuala Belait",""]],"22":[[1,"48","7","National Energy Policy Development","Developing an energy policy that helps the oil and gas industry and give due consideration to the need to help develop new industries, including downstream activities, food processing, medical, logistics, financial services, tourism, ICT and others.",""],[1,"101","2","Electricity Generation Capacity Expansion and Grid Strengthening","The government will continue to ensure sufficient, high quality and reliable electricity supply by increasing the generation capacity and strengthening the transmission and distribution systems.",""],[1,"101","2","Private Sector Electricity Generation Participation","Apart from the government, the role of the private sector will be enhanced in generating electricity to meet the demand in the country.",""],[1,"125","1","Reliable Electricity Supply Provision","The government's target for zero blackout can be achieved through the provision of a reliable electricity supply.",""],[1,"125","2","Combined Cycle Power Plant Utilisation","the utilisation of the combined cycle power plant will continue to take place in the years to come",""],[1,"125","2","Solar Panel Installation for Households","The use of solar panels as one of the original energy-saving alternatives will also be implemented, as evidenced by the installation of 100 solar panels to 65 houses in Kampong Ayer",""],[1,"125","2","Energy Conservation Research Initiative","the government has identified, and will continue to identify through research, on effective ways of energy use for the country",""],[1,"164","6","Lumut Power Station Rejuvenation Works, Power Renew and Upgrade","Lumut Power Station Rejuvenation Works Power Renew and Upgrade",""],[1,"164","8","Gadong 2 Power Station Expansion and 11kV/415V Reinforcement","Extension toExpansion of Gadong 2 Power Station Reinforcement of 11KV/415V Daerah Brunei Muara District",""],[1,"165","1","Electricity Network Reinforcement Projects","Reinforcement of 11KV/415V Daerah Kuala Belait District Reinforcement of 11KV/415V Daerah Temburong District Reinforcement of Twin Circuits 66kV from 66/11kV Substesen Mentiri to 66kV/11kV",""],[1,"165","2","Electricity Supply Network Asset Replacement and Inventory Management System","Strategic Reinforcement and Replacement of Cable, Switchgears, Ring Main Unit & Transformers Electricity Supply Network Asset/Inventory Management and Data Procurement System",""],[1,"165","3","66kV Transmission Overhead Line Upgrade","Upgrading of 66kV Transmission Overhead Line between GPS 1 and Tutong 66kV S/S",""],[1,"165","4","66kV Transmission Line Upgrade between GPS 1 and Muara Substation","Upgrading of 66kV Transmission Overhead Line between GPS 1 and Muara 66kV S/S",""]],"23":[[1,"29","7","Business Registration Simplification","i) Fast and easy process for starting a business;",""],[1,"29","7","Business Capacity and Capability Strengthening","ii) Strong business capacity and capabilities;",""],[1,"29","7","Intellectual Property Rights Protection","iii) Protection of Intellectual Property Rights.",""],[1,"49","10","Government Procedure and Regulatory Streamlining Reform","Streamlining government procedures and regulations to enable prompt decision-making, the provision of high quality public services and the minimisation of red tape.",""],[1,"50","1","SME and Entrepreneur Business Skills and Financing Support Programme","Introducing well-designed and well- funded programmes and more effective ways of financing local enterprises to help local small and medium enterprises (SME) and entrepreneurs gain business skills and become more competitive at regional and international levels.",""],[1,"50","2","Incubation Centres for SMEs and Entrepreneurs","Developing incubation centres to assist and promote local SMEs and entrepreneurs in areas such as ICT.",""],[1,"50","3","Foreign Direct Investment Linkages for Local SMEs and Entrepreneurs","34. Maximising the benefits of foreign direct investments for local SME and entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"50","4","Local Procurement Promotion for Businesses and Industries","Encouraging major businesses and industries to use local products, suppliers and contractors.",""],[1,"50","6","Government Procedure Simplification for SMEs and Entrepreneurs","Reducing the cost of doing business for local SMEs and entrepreneurs by simplifying government procedures.",""],[1,"50","7","Prompt Government Decision and Payment Mechanism for Local Contractors and Suppliers","Ensuring prompt government decisions and payment to local contractors and suppliers.",""],[1,"57","2","Foreign Direct Investment Attraction","These efforts include attracting foreign direct investments, stimulating entrepreneurial activities and enhancing knowledge, expertise and innovation.",""],[1,"57","2","Entrepreneurship Promotion","These efforts include attracting foreign direct investments, stimulating entrepreneurial activities and enhancing knowledge, expertise and innovation.",""],[1,"63","6","Business Start-up and Investment Streamlining Reform","The government through relevant agencies will focus on efforts to promote the following: innovation and the use of advanced technology; capacity building through investments in human resource development; research activities which can be commercialised; and streamlining processes to better facilitate the start-up of businesses and investments in the country.",""],[1,"106","1","Business Environment Improvement Measures","The government through relevant agencies will continue to emphasise on aspects such as; the process to start a business, strengthen the capacity and capability of businesses and protect of copyrights and intellectual property rights.",""],[1,"106","5","Business Start-Up Process Simplification","the government through the relevant agencies will ensure that processes and procedures to start a business will continue to be simplified and speeded up.",""],[1,"106","6","Online Business Licensing System","The introduction of the Online Business Licensing System is one example of the government's efforts to ease the process of starting a business in the country.",""],[1,"106","6","Ease of Doing Business Committee","The establishment of the Ease of Doing Business Committee is also an evidence of the government's commitment to continue to provide an environment conducive to local and foreign investors.",""],[1,"118","6","Ease of Doing Business Committee","The setting up of the Ease of Doing Business Committee and the Authority of Building and Construction Industry (ABCi) are part of the initiatives carried out to integrate the functions",""],[1,"106","6","Authority of Building and Construction Industry Coordination Function","The government has also established the Authority of Building and Construction Industry (ABCi) which has the role of coordinating and processing applications for building and land development for residential, commercial and industrial purposes.",""],[1,"108","1","Business-Friendly Regulatory Review for Start-Up Facilitation","Procedures including existing laws will continue to be reviewed from time to time to ensure that they are more business-friendly that help facilitate and expedite the process of starting a business.",""],[1,"108","2","Private Sector and SME Strengthening Initiative","Strengthening the private sector including the small and medium enterprises is important in order to accelerate economic growth.",""],[1,"108","2","Ease of Doing Business Improvement Effort","Hence, it is important to focus on efforts to improve the country's position or ranking in the Ease of Doing Business index.",""],[1,"118","6","Authority of Building and Construction Industry (ABCi)","The setting up of the Ease of Doing Business Committee and the Authority of Building and Construction Industry (ABCi) are part of the initiatives carried out to integrate the functions",""]],"24":[[1,"30","1","Knowledge and High-Technology Investment Promotion","The fourth thrust is a Productive and Progressive Economy Based on Knowledge and Innovation, which leads to the generation of a high and sustainable economic growth through investments in knowledge and high technology innovation, as well as non-oil and gas exports in efforts to diversify the economy.",""],[1,"30","1","Knowledge-Based Infrastructure and Facilities Development","This thrust covers five main factors: i) Knowledge-based infrastructure and facilities; ii) Research and development (R&D) that have a commercial value; iii) High technology private investments; iv) Entrepreneurship development; and v) Non-oil and gas investment and exports.",""],[1,"30","1","Commercial R&D Support","This thrust covers five main factors: i) Knowledge-based infrastructure and facilities; ii) Research and development (R&D) that have a commercial value; iii) High technology private investments; iv) Entrepreneurship development; and v) Non-oil and gas investment and exports.",""],[1,"30","1","High-Technology Private Investment Promotion","This thrust covers five main factors: i) Knowledge-based infrastructure and facilities; ii) Research and development (R&D) that have a commercial value; iii) High technology private investments; iv) Entrepreneurship development; and v) Non-oil and gas investment and exports.",""],[1,"63","6","Innovation and Advanced Technology Promotion","The government through relevant agencies will focus on efforts to promote the following: innovation and the use of advanced technology; capacity building through investments in human resource development; research activities which can be commercialised; and streamlining processes to better facilitate the start-up of businesses and investments in the country.",""],[1,"63","6","Commercialisation of Research Activities","The government through relevant agencies will focus on efforts to promote the following: innovation and the use of advanced technology; capacity building through investments in human resource development; research activities which can be commercialised; and streamlining processes to better facilitate the start-up of businesses and investments in the country.",""],[1,"76","1","Productivity Enhancement through Technology and Innovation Investment","the enhancement of productivity in the public and private sectors through the use of latest technologies and investments in knowledge and innovation.",""],[1,"76","4","Integrated National Productivity Enhancement Measures","Towards this end, the national development planning must support integrated measures that can encourage such increase in productivity.",""],[1,"76","5","Innovation Incentives and Assistance Package","Relevant incentives and assistance must be thought out so that we can encourage innovation, the use of latest technologies, capacity building including investments in human resource development, increasing research activities that can be commercialised, and facilitating investments and exports activities in the country ...",""],[1,"78","3","Human Resource Investment, Research and Innovation Support, and Technology Adoption","This includes continuing substantial investment in human resource and investment in research and innovation and by supporting the use of latest technologies.",""],[1,"78","4","Knowledge and Innovation Productivity Enhancement Initiative","RKN10 will give priority to exploring approaches for increasing productivity through the use of knowledge and innovation.",""],[1,"78","5","Knowledge and Innovation Capacity Development","The concept of knowledge and innovation emphasised in RKN10 focuses on the generation of high productivity through increasing knowledge, skills and competency of the workforce in strategic areas; increasing research activities that have high commercial value; and instilling the culture of innovation and creativity among the local youth.",""],[1,"79","3","Public-Private Research and Development Partnership","the public sector to work in partnership with higher learning institutions and to get commitment from the private sector to be actively engaged in research and development (R&D).",""],[1,"79","3","Enabling Environment for Research","A more conducive environment for research will be put in place to further encourage research activities which can produce commercially viable output.",""],[1,"80","1","Special Funds for Research and Development and Human Resource Development","special funds for R&D as well as for Human Resource Development have been established to ensure that knowledge-based economic activities and innovation can be enhanced.",""],[1,"92","2","Research and Development Fund","the government has allocated a special fund known as the Research and Development Fund (R&D Fund) to encourage research activities in various fields.",""],[1,"137","10","Research and Development Fund","Under the Research and Development (R&D) Fund, the government has allocated a total of BND200 million to expand research activities in the country.",""],[1,"112","1","Knowledge and Innovation for Productivity and Diversification","Knowledge and innovation will be part of the strategic mechanisms that will help the country to accomplish economic diversification.",""],[1,"113","2","R&D, Innovation, and Technology Skills Investment","Investments will thus be focused on enhancing R&D, innovation, creativity and skills in technology.",""],[1,"113","4","Private Investment Attraction in High-Technology Industries","Continuous efforts will be undertaken to attract private investments in high technology industries.",""],[1,"113","5","Public-Private Commercialisation Support for Local Entrepreneurs","Cooperation between the private sector and the government in commercialising ideas and models created by local entrepreneurs will encourage greater involvement of locals in the field of entrepreneurship, especially in the field of creative industries.",""],[1,"113","5","Private Investment in Technology Promotion","Private investments in technology in various sectors are not only for domestic consumption, but also represent new source of exports for the country.",""],[1,"115","3","Productivity Enhancement and Innovation-Led Growth Initiative","Efforts to increase productivity will need to be spearheaded by knowledge and innovation.",""],[1,"115","3","Knowledge-Based Industry Development","the development of knowledge- based industries will be the focused of RKN10.",""],[1,"135","9","Technology and Innovation Promotion Projects","Projects which promote the use of new technology and contribute to enhancing innovation and increasing productivity of the country.",""],[1,"159","15","Calibration and Testing Laboratory Establishment","Establishment of Calibration and Testing Laboratory of the National Standards Centre",""],[1,"168","2","Central Research Laboratories Feasibility Study","Feasibility Study on Central Research Laboratories",""],[1,"169","11","Radio Frequency Identification Technology Development Program","Radio Frequency Identification (RFID) Technology Development Program",""]],"25":[[1,"163","5","Construction of Forestry Department Housing Blocks in Andulau","Construction of 2 Blocks of Housing for Forestry Department in Andulau (Class F Flats - 6 units/blocks)",""],[1,"163","6","Construction of Agricultural Department Flats","Construction of 3 Flats (6 units) for Agriculture Depatment",""],[1,"163","7","Construction of Government Housing Flats for Postal Service Department","Construction of Government Housing Flats for Postal Service Department - Limau Manis",""],[1,"167","1","Public Buildings and Government Facilities Construction Programme","Fire Station at Kampong Petani, Tutong New Building for Department of Environment, Parks and Recreation and Department of Town and Country Planning New Building for Department of Sanitation and Drainage New Building for Electrical Services Office Pusar Ulak and Bunut Branch Anti Corruption Bureau Building Department of Labour Headquarters Building Brunei Museums Deparment Headquarters Building Temburong District Office Building Building for Royal Customs and Excise Department, Belait District Building for Department of Economic Planning and Development Building for Embassies and High Commissions Abroad Building for Brunei Embassy Complex in Japan Religious Activities Centre and Office, Temburong District Customs Office Building Sungai Tujoh Royal Customs and Excise Building, Sungai Lampai Extension to Information Department Headquarters Building Extension to Brunei Muara District Office Building Extension to Islamic Propagation Centre Building Upgrading of State Store Building Complex, Gadong Upgrading of Language and Literature Bureau Library Building, Bandar Seri Begawan",""],[1,"167","2","Public Buildings Construction and Refurbishment Programme","Refurbishment of Public Works Department Headquarters Upgrading of Pulaie Welfare Home Complex Office of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade Construction of 1 Additional Block for Ministry of Health Fire Station and Housing - Kampong Bukit Beruang and Kampong Mentiri Construction of Courts Building Tutong District Land Transport Department Complex - Belait District Branch Construction of Prime Minister's Office Building Complex Brunei Embassy Complex in Jakarta, Indonesia including Office, Official and Staff Residence",""],[1,"170","4","Officers Mess Renovation and Banquet Hall Construction","Renovation of Officers Mess, Royal Brunei Police Force and Banquet Hall Construction C.Q.B. Range",""]],"26":[[1,"47","1","Continuous Coordination and Development of Development Strategies and Policy Directions","eight strategies and fifty policy directions for development will continuously be coordinated and developed by the government, the private sector and relevant organisations, and will be implemented more efficiently as listed below :-",""],[1,"30","7","Introduction of New Regulations for RKN10 Implementation","In ensuring that the RKN10 will be implemented soundly and on target, new regulations have been introduced which have to be complied with by all ministries.",""],[1,"30","6","Alternative Financing for Commercially Viable Projects","The Government will also explore the use of alternative financing for projects that have a commercial value in order to encourage private sector involvement in the development of the economy through the public-private partnership model.",""],[1,"48","8","Public Service Privatization and Accountability Reform","Encourage projects that have elements of value for money to be more resilient and accountable, including the privatisation of government services that have been identified as being more effectively carried out by the private sector.",""],[1,"50","5","Privatisation, Commercialisation, and Outsourcing of Government Services","Privatising, commercialising and outsourcing of appropriate government services as a way of expanding business opportunities for local SMEs and entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"118","1","Institutional Development Strategy for Good Governance","the Institutional Development Strategy has been outlined under the Outline of Strategies and Policies for Development (OSPD) 2007-2017 to ensure that government institutions maintain high standards of good governance in the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"119","2","Civil Service Excellence and Integrity Strengthening","Efforts to enhance excellence in the government's administrative machinery will focus on realising the 21st Century Civil Service Vision.",""],[1,"119","2","Continuous Civil Servant Training Programme","Civil servants will be given continuous training in various fields, through courses and conferences, held locally and abroad.",""],[1,"119","2","Civil Service Integrity and Values Reinforcement","The instillation of Islamic values and spiritual aspects will also be inculcated and incorporated as part of efforts to strengthen the integrity of the civil service.",""],[1,"119","3","Legislative Review and Legal Reform","One of the ways this is achieved is through the enactment of new laws and the amendment of existing laws based on international best practices.",""],[1,"119","5","Public Sector Regulatory Framework for Service Streamlining","the formulation of a regulatory framework that can streamline work procedures and systems, particularly in the provision of services to the general public.",""],[1,"120","1","Civil Service Modernisation and Governance Improvement","continuing efforts will be carried out to ensure that the goals of good governance and government modernisation are met, namely the creation of a more efficient, productive, high-quality and modern civil service.",""],[1,"120","2","Public-Private Cooperation Strengthening","A close and integrated cooperation among government agencies and the private sector should also be strengthened in order to increase productivity and economic growth, while at the same time enabling the government to take heed of the needs of the private sector.",""],[1,"119","4","Legislative and Regulatory Reform Package","Part of those efforts include the enactment and amendment of several acts and regulations such as the Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Order, 2011; the Patents Order, 2011; the Monetary Authority of Brunei Darussalam (AMBD) Order, 2010; the Employment Order, 2009; the Investment Incentives Order, 2001; the Miscellaneous Licences Act; and the Price Control Act.",""]],"27":[[1,"49","3","Military Infrastructure Development and Procurement Reform","Implementing new approaches to the development of military infrastructure and to procurement in order to ensure greater efficiency and cost effectiveness, including, where appropriate, through PPP.",""],[1,"170","1","Armed Forces Infrastructure and Training Facilities Development Package","Feasibility Study for Artillery Regiment Feasibility Study for Regiment Armour Master Plan for Temburong Camp Fourth Batallion Study on the Rebuilding of Berakas Garrison Future Explosive Ordinance Training Area Special Force Regiment Camp - Phase I Development of Military Academy",""],[1,"170","2","Ammunition Storage Expansion Phase II","Expansion of Ammunition Storage - Phase II",""]],"28":[[1,"133","1","RKN10 Project Review, Approval, and Monitoring Process","reviewing and evaluating the report of proposed new projects, as well as projects that have been carried forward from RKN 2007-2012 which had been approved by the Sub-Committee II; identifying matters that required improvements to ensure that each project could achieve the goals of Wawasan Brunei 2035 and was in line with the theme of the RKN10; and monitoring the preparation of draft reports to ensure that the RKN10 report would be completed within the stipulated time",""],[1,"133","4","Project Evaluation and Budget Allocation Sub-Committee","Sub-Committee II was formed with the purpose of evaluating proposed projects and of making recommendations and budget allocation for those projects, based on selection criteria such as the project's contribution to economic growth and the capacity of the ministries to implement the projects.",""],[1,"133","5","Ministry Project Appraisal and Review Working Groups","Working groups responsible for each ministry had also been formed within the Department of Economic Planning and Development, tasked with collecting, enlisting and reviewing all project applications and proposed budget allocation received from ministries.",""],[1,"137","1","Implementation of Already Approved Projects","Prior to submitting any new project applications, the ministry must implement projects that have already been approved;",""],[1,"137","2","Resubmission of Approved Projects Without Budget Allocation","Projects which have been approved without any budget allocation must be re-submitted to the Department of Economic Planning and Development after the required project scope and actual price have been obtained;",""],[1,"137","4","Research Project Submission and Endorsement Mechanism","Research-oriented projects must be submitted to the Brunei Research Council (BRC) for assessment and endorsement;",""],[1,"137","6","ICT Project Assessment and Endorsement Requirement","Information and Communication Technology (ICT) projects must be submitted to the E-Government National Centre (EGNC) for assessment and endorsement;",""],[1,"137","7","PFI and PPP Project Assessment and Endorsement Mechanism","Potential projects for implementation through Private Finance Initiative (PFI) and Public-Private Partnership (PPP) must be submitted to the Department of Economic Planning and Development for assessment and endorsement;","Department of Economic Planning and Development"]],"51":[[1,"29","5","Teacher Quality Improvement","Quality teachers;",""],[1,"90","1","Teacher Training for Holistic Education","Teachers will thus be given training focusing on a holistic education which is aimed at producing intelligent, competent, charismatic and versatile students.",""],[1,"90","2","Teachers' Service Scheme","the government has also introduced a scheme for teachers called the 'Skim Perkhidmatan Perguruan' or the Teachers' Service Scheme on 1st June 2008.",""],[1,"90","3","Teacher ICT Competency and Skills Strengthening","Various efforts and initiatives have also been implemented to strengthen ICT competencies and skills among teachers.",""]],"52":[[1,"90","6","Technical and Vocational Education Scholarship Scheme","The introduction of the Technical and Vocational Education Scholarship Scheme (BPTV) at the local private institutions on 15th July 2011 provides opportunities for local school leavers who have completed their 'O' and 'A' levels or its equivalent to pursue higher education.",""],[1,"93","2","International Education Institution Investment and Establishment Initiative","the government also welcomes greater collaboration from international institutions abroad to invest and establish their institutions in this country, and not only offering twinning programmes in existing local institutions.",""],[1,"93","2","Twinning Programme Expansion in Local Institutions","the government also welcomes greater collaboration from international institutions abroad to invest and establish their institutions in this country, and not only offering twinning programmes in existing local institutions.",""]],"53":[[1,"37","6","Brunei Entrepreneurial Education Scheme","BEES - Brunei Entrepreneurial Education Scheme",""],[1,"29","5","Entrepreneurial Education Promotion","Entrepreneurial education;",""],[1,"30","1","Entrepreneurship Development Initiative","This thrust covers five main factors: i) Knowledge-based infrastructure and facilities; ii) Research and development (R&D) that have a commercial value; iii) High technology private investments; iv) Entrepreneurship development; and v) Non-oil and gas investment and exports.",""],[1,"91","3","Entrepreneurial Education Integration in School Curriculum","One of the efforts implemented recently in 2012 is the integration of entrepreneurial education as part of the school curriculum through the Business, Arts and Technology (BAT) subjects provided in Year 7 and Year 8.",""],[1,"91","5","Early Entrepreneurial Education Introduction","The introduction of entrepreneurial education at an early stage is expected to help stimulate, educate and nurture students to be more attracted to, and understand, the concept and practice of entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"91","6","Entrepreneurship Placement Programme","the 'Program Penempatan Membentuk Rebung Keusahawanan' (Entrepreneurship Placement Programme) implemented by the Ministry of Industry and Primary Resources","Ministry of Industry and Primary Resources"],[1,"91","6","Business School Establishment","and the setting up of the Business School",""],[1,"91","7","Entrepreneurial Training Programme","The private sector is also providing entrepreneurial training programmes such as the LiveWire programme which has been on-going since 2001 and is funded entirely by the Brunei Shell Petroleum Company Sdn Bhd.",""],[1,"92","1","Entrepreneurship Development Programmes","the Brunei Economic Development Board (BEDB) is also actively developing and implementing various programmes to encourage positive growth and development of entrepreneurship in the country.",""],[1,"51","6","Entrepreneurship and Self-Reliance Promotion Programmes","Strengthening programmes which will foster the spirit of entrepreneurship and self- reliance among our people.",""]],"54":[[1,"10","2","Strengthen Research Activities in Higher Education and Other Sectors","pertinent research activities need to be intensified in higher education institutions and in other sectors so as to enable the discovery of new and more effective approaches",""],[1,"47","7","Research, Development and Innovation Promotion","Promoting research, development and innovation both in government- funded institutions and through public-private partnerships (PPP) and international partnerships.",""],[1,"92","5","Higher Education Research and Development Collaboration","local higher learning institutions are encouraged to have closer collaboration with the private sector as well as foreign institutions to conduct and undertake more research activities.",""]],"55":[[1,"30","3","High-Quality and Sustainable Development Infrastructure","The sixth thrust is a High Quality and Sustainable Development Infrastructure.",""],[1,"51","1","Social Infrastructure Provision Programme","Providing adequate social infrastructure particularly in the provision of public housing, transport and communication, health care and education.",""],[1,"51","2","Legal and Regulatory Frameworks for Social and Industrial Infrastructure Investment","Adopting appropriate legal and regulatory frameworks to promote investments in social and industrial infrastructure, including privatisation and PPP in line with international best practices.",""]],"57":[[1,"49","1","Integrated National Security Coordination","Promoting close coordination between Brunei Darussalam's diplomatic, defence and intelligence institutions to ensure an integrated approach to national security.",""],[1,"49","2","Security Forces Professionalization and Modernization","Strengthening the security forces, including the armed forces, the police and intelligence agencies, so that they are distinguished by high standards of professionalism, training and technological expertise.",""],[1,"49","4","Good Governance Promotion Initiative","Promoting good governance in both the public and private sectors with particular emphasis on honesty and accountability to ensure public confidence and trust.",""],[1,"49","7","Judicial System Strengthening and Legal Clarity Reform","Ensuring a modern legal system that is clear in its provisions and application, and a judiciary system that ensures independence, fairness and impartiality.",""],[1,"49","11","Independent Ombudsman Institution","Creating new institutions such as an independent ombudsman to ensure accountability in the public and private sectors.",""]],"58":[[1,"49","5","Emergency Response Systems and Organizations Development","Developing further appropriate systems and organisations for responding quickly and effectively to threats from natural disasters, infectious diseases, acts of terrorism and other emergencies.",""]],"62":[[1,"48","3","Capital Market Development and Sukuk Financing Initiative","Creating a strong capital market, including the Islamic bond market (sukuk), to help finance economic growth.",""]],"63":[[1,"51","10","Cultural and Historical Heritage Maintenance Guidelines","Establishing clear guidelines for the proper maintenance of buildings and landmarks of cultural and historical value.",""]],"64":[[1,"30","1","Non-Oil and Gas Export Diversification","The fourth thrust is a Productive and Progressive Economy Based on Knowledge and Innovation, which leads to the generation of a high and sustainable economic growth through investments in knowledge and high technology innovation, as well as non-oil and gas exports in efforts to diversify the economy.",""],[1,"48","5","Downstream Industry and Non-Oil Sector Investment Promotion","Promoting investments in downstream industries and other non-oil and gas sectors to generate economic growth and assist in the diversification of economic activity.",""],[1,"61","4","Oil and Gas Mega Projects Implementation","Job opportunities are expected to increase with the implementation of mega projects in the oil and gas sector.",""]],"65":[[1,"58","9","Price Control and Basic Goods Subsidy Measures","the impact of higher import prices on domestic inflation was averted through the enforcement of the Price Control Act, the provision of subsidies on basic goods and utilities, and other administrative procedures.",""],[1,"96","7","Measures to Increase Economic Participation","the government will continue to adopt various measures to increase the level of economic participation of all levels of society.",""],[1,"96","8","Extended Maternity Leave Entitlement","changes to the period of maternity entitlement leave from 56 days to 105 days have already been implemented.",""],[1,"97","2","Continuous Assistance for Senior Citizens","Senior citizens in the country will also be given continuous assistance by the government, in terms of monetary and specialised services.",""]],"66":[[1,"97","2","Old-Age Pension Payment Alignment","One of the initiatives which was implemented in January 2012 was the alignment of the day in paying old-aged pension with payment of the monthly salary of the civil service.",""],[1,"97","3","Government Assistance for Special Needs Independence and NGO Support","The special needs group is also given assistance by the government to enable them to be independent and live harmoniously within the society.",""],[1,"97","3","NGO Land Site Incentive for Special Needs Support","As an incentive, special assistance in terms of land sites provision will be given to the NGOs by the government.",""]],"67":[[1,"97","7","Five Thematic Health Strategies","the government has prepared five new thematic strategies as outlined in the Ministry of Health's Vision 2035 Health Strategy Book.","Ministry of Health"],[1,"98","2","Public Health Awareness and Healthy Lifestyle Promotion","In RKN10, focus is given to enhancing public awareness on cleanliness and healthcare and on practicing the concept of `prevention is better than cure'.",""],[1,"98","2","Healthy Diet and Physical Activity Promotion","The public will also be urged to practise a healthy lifestyle by emphasising a healthy and balanced diet, maintaining cleanliness and involving in physical activities.",""],[1,"98","3","Health Treatment Facilities and New Technology Adoption","the government will continue to provide the required facilities for appropriate treatment and increase the use of new technologies.",""],[1,"98","4","Health Workforce Skills and Specialist Training Programme","the skills and expertise of the human resources in the health sector will be further strengthened and improved.",""],[1,"98","7","Private Sector Participation in Health and Medical Services","The government will also continue to encourage greater involvement of the private sector in the provision of health and medical services particularly in sectors such as dentistry, optometry and others.",""]],"68":[[1,"99","1","Environmental Legislation Enforcement and Solid Waste Management","This includes a more efficient use of national resources, the provision and enforcement of relevant legislations, effective solid waste management and assuring our national commitments are in line with international best practices.",""],[1,"99","2","Environmental Legal Framework Development","The formulation of a legal framework related to the environment that includes environmental impact assessments, environmental pollution control and hazardous chemical waste control is expected to be completed in 2012.",""],[1,"99","2","Hazardous Chemicals Waste Treatment Centre Feasibility Study","A feasibility study for the construction of a waste treatment and disposal centre for hazardous chemicals is expected to be completed too in the same year.",""],[1,"99","3","Integrated Waste Management System in Sungai Akar","efforts such as an integrated waste management system in Sungai Akar",""],[1,"99","3","Engineered Landfill Disposal Site in Sungai Paku, Tutong","an engineered landfill disposal site in Sungai Paku, Tutong have been implemented",""],[1,"99","4","Waste Recycling Rate Increase Measure","measures will also be focused towards waste reduction by increasing recycling rates relative to the production of waste from about 5 per cent to 10 per cent by 2015.",""],[1,"99","4","Hazardous Waste Management Review","The management of toxic and hazardous wastes from government and private sectors using the incineration method will also be reviewed.",""],[1,"99","5","Air and Water Quality Monitoring and Enforcement Upgrade","the existing monitoring systems and quality management frameworks will be upgraded.",""],[1,"100","1","Multi-stakeholder Environmental Protection Cooperation","Apart from the government, the private sector, NGOs and the general public are also encouraged to play a role in ensuring that the environment is protected.",""],[1,"100","1","International Environmental Best-Practice Cooperation","Cooperation with international organisations will also be enhanced in order to get the best practices to ensure for a protected environment.",""],[1,"163","13","Development of New Waste Disposal Site in Brunei Muara Area","Development of New Waste Diposal Site in Brunei Muara Area",""],[1,"163","14","New Waste Disposal Site Development in Temburong","Development of New Waste Diposal Site in Temburong Area Cleaning up of Brunei River",""],[1,"168","2","Integrated Hazardous and Toxic Waste Treatment and Disposal System Feasibility Study","Feasibility Study on the Construction of Integrated Hazardous and Toxic Waste Treatment and Disposal System",""]],"69":[[1,"100","4","Youth Civic Values and Development Programmes","the government will continue to inculcate early awareness among the youths on the values of the national philosophy, culture and conduct based on the Malay Islamic Monarchy.",""],[1,"100","4","National Youth Service","The National Youth Service (PKBN) and the provision of youth development programmes are some of the measures that have been initiated by the government.",""],[1,"100","4","Youth Development Programmes","The National Youth Service (PKBN) and the provision of youth development programmes are some of the measures that have been initiated by the government.",""],[1,"164","1","Youth Development Centre Workshops Construction","Construction of 2 Multipurpose Workshops at the Youth Development Centre",""],[1,"164","1","Youth Development Centre Field and Running Track","Field and Running Track for the Youth Development Centre",""],[1,"164","1","Youth Park Construction at Hassanal Bolkiah National Sports Complex","Construction of Youth Park at the Hassanal Bolkiah National Sports Complex",""],[1,"167","4","Youth Development Centre Phase III Facilities Retention and Rehabilitation","Youth Development Centre Phase III - Facilities and Infrastructure Retention and Rehabilitation Centre, Internal Security Department Extension to Printing Department Building",""]],"70":[[1,"100","5","Security Agency Professionalization and Technology Training","the government will continue to strengthen its security-related agencies such as the Royal Brunei Armed Forces, the Royal Brunei Police Force and other intelligence agencies so as to enhance their professionalism and to adequately provide staff with training and expertise in latest technologies.",""],[1,"100","6","Public Participation in Crime Prevention","The government will continue to ensure public involvement in assisting the authorities at the national level to combat crime and other threats.",""],[1,"100","6","Regional and International Security Cooperation","Meanwhile, closer cooperation at the regional and international level will continue to be improved in order to ensure safety, peace, stability and prosperity of the nation as a whole can be achieved.",""],[1,"164","1","Multipurpose Hall for Narcotics Control Bureau","Construction of Multipurpose Hall for Narcotics Control Bureau",""]],"71":[[1,"101","1","Public Facilities Access Expansion","In order to achieve a high quality of life, the government will provide access to public facilities such as water and electricity, as well as transport and communication.",""]],"72":[[1,"101","3","Energy Tariff Reform","the government has enforced a new tariff effective January 2012",""],[1,"101","3","Government-Financed Pre-Paid Meter Replacement","the government has replaced post-paid meters to pre-paid meters installed at no cost in private houses and financed entirely by the government",""]],"73":[[1,"101","6","Road Construction and Upgrade Programme","These include the construction and upgrading of roads such as the construction of an 18.6 kilometre road in the Telisai-Lumut area which will be completed in 2013 and the construction of interchanges at identified areas; upgrading of the Brunei International Airport and enhancement of broad band infrastructure.",""],[1,"125","4","Highway Construction and Flyover and Bridge Development","the ongoing construction of highways and the consideration for the construction of several flyovers and bridges are some of the other efforts undertaken to ensure users' comfort and to reduce road congestions.",""],[1,"160","3","Bridge and Link Road Construction","Bridge and Link Road from Old Airport Area to Menglait Jerudong-Tungku Link Road",""],[1,"160","4","Tanah Jambu Link Road Phase II Flyover Bridge Construction","Tanah Jambu Link Road - Phase II Construction of Flyover Bridge at Highway Junction",""],[1,"160","5","Road and Bridge Construction and Upgrading Programme","Study on the Construction of Roads and Bridges Linking Brunei-Muara and Temburong District Seria By-Pass Dual Carriageways Third Carriageway on Sultan Haji Hassanal Bolkiah Highway Upgrading and Widening of Primary Roads Upgrading and Repair of Road Dividers and Access Roads Upgrading of Bridges Upgrading of Bridges - Phase II Rehabilitation of Asphalt Roads in Brunei Muara District",""],[1,"160","9","Slip Road Construction to UBD Campus","Construction of Slip Road at Tungku Link Flyover towards Universiti Brunei Darussalam (UBD) Campus",""],[1,"160","10","Roundabout Slip Road Construction near Jame `Asr Kampong Kiarong","Construction of Roundabout Slip Road near Jame `Asr Kampong Kiarong",""],[1,"160","10","Tutong-Seria Road Construction, Stage 3","Construction of Tutong - Seria Road, Stage 3",""],[1,"160","10","Telisai-Lumut Link Road Construction","Telisai - Lumut Link Road",""],[1,"160","10","Sungai Kebun-Residency Road Bridge Link Construction","Construction of Bridge Link from Sungai Kebun to Residency Road",""],[1,"160","11","Flyover Construction at Jln Gadong / Jln Telanai Junction","Construction of Flyover at Jln Gadong / Jln Telanai Junction",""],[1,"168","8","Muara-Tutong Highway Interchange Construction","Local Plans for Mukim Construction of Interchange at Muara - Tutong Highway / Meragang Housing Production of Hydrographic Paper Navigational Chart and Electronic Navigational Chart",""]],"74":[[1,"101","6","Airport Upgrade and Broadband Expansion","These include the construction and upgrading of roads such as the construction of an 18.6 kilometre road in the Telisai-Lumut area which will be completed in 2013 and the construction of interchanges at identified areas; upgrading of the Brunei International Airport and enhancement of broad band infrastructure.",""],[1,"125","5","Brunei International Airport Terminal Modernisation and Runway Widening","The terminal modernisation and widening of the airport runway at the Brunei International Airport",""],[1,"125","5","Muara Port Capacity Expansion","the expansion of the capacity of Muara Port",""],[1,"160","13","Runway Rehabilitation at Brunei International Airport","Rehabilitation of Runway at Brunei International Airport",""],[1,"160","14","Airport Security Control Equipment Upgrade","Upgrading of Security Control Equipments at Brunei International Airport Setting Up of X-Ray Access Control Machines at Airport Employees Entry Point",""],[1,"161","1","Airport and Aerodrome Facilities Improvement","Infrastructure Development Plan, Improvement of Airport / Aerodrome Facilities and Services Transformation of Brunei International Airport",""],[1,"161","2","Inland Container Depot and Container Port Security Building Repair and Cleaning","Inland Container Depot (ICD) including Repairing and Cleaning Container Port Security Building",""],[1,"161","3","Harbour Tug and Aluminium Pilot Launch Extension","Pull Harbour Tug and Aluminium Pilot Launch Extension of the Department of Ports Headquarters Building Additional Sailing Signs at Temburong River Supply of Container Handling Forklift and Primemovers with Trailers Service and Export Hub, Muara Port Additional/Extension of 150-200 Container Berth/Wharf at Muara Container Terminal (MCT) Additional Quay Crane for New Additional Container Berth at MCT Structural Integrity Test for Muara Port Wharf",""],[1,"159","16","Sg Liang Jetty Construction","Construction of Sg Liang Jetty Incubation and Primary Resource Excellence Management Increasing Compliance to International Standards by Local SMEs Provision of Tourism Industry Facilities",""],[1,"168","8","Hydrographic Navigational Chart Production","Local Plans for Mukim Construction of Interchange at Muara - Tutong Highway / Meragang Housing Production of Hydrographic Paper Navigational Chart and Electronic Navigational Chart",""]],"75":[[1,"101","6","Public Transport Improvement Programme","In order to increase the usage of public transport services, all aspects of public transportation such as connectivity, efficiency and service standard will be improved.",""],[1,"99","6","Integrated Transport System Feasibility Study","a feasibility study for an Integrated Transport System will also be conducted.",""],[1,"163","12","Bus and Taxi Terminal Upgrading","Upgrading of Bus and Taxi Terminal, Seria",""],[1,"164","1","Bus Terminal Construction","Construction of Bus Terminal",""],[1,"125","4","BSB Master Plan for Communication and Transportation System","The BSB Master Plan has been prepared with the objective of providing Bandar Seri Begawan with an efficient communication and transportation system.",""]],"76":[[1,"102","1","Cultural Infrastructure Improvement","The provision of cultural infrastructure that aim to exhibit the culture and heritage of Brunei Darussalam will continue to be improved.",""],[1,"102","2","Sports and Recreational Infrastructure Improvement and Expansion","Efforts have been undertaken to improve the existing infrastructure and to provide additional sports facilities.",""],[1,"102","3","Private Sector Participation in Cultural and Recreational Infrastructure","the involvement and contribution of the private sector in the provision of such infrastructures will continue to be encouraged.",""],[1,"164","1","Maritime Museum Display Development","Display for Maritime Museum",""],[1,"164","1","Pantai Serasa Recreational Development","Pantai Serasa Recreational Development",""],[1,"164","1","Tutong Central Area Improvements","Tutong Central Area Improvements",""],[1,"160","1","Kampong Ayer Cultural and Tourism Centre","Kampong Ayer Cultural and Tourism Centre",""]],"77":[[1,"107","1","Entrepreneur and Business Capacity Strengthening Programme","the improving and strengthening of the capacity and capability of entrepreneurs and businesses to expand and later penetrate the international market",""],[1,"107","2","Local Business Capacity-Building and Entrepreneurship Training","Conducting workshops, courses and entrepreneurship training are some of the examples of several efforts made to increase the capacity and capability of local businesses in the country.",""],[1,"108","2","Entrepreneur Business Training and Financial Assistance Programme","Furthermore, various programmes including business management courses and financial assistance will continue to be provided to potential entrepreneurs and businesses.",""],[1,"114","1","Knowledge and Innovation Entrepreneurship Support","the government will continue to provide support for entrepreneurship based on knowledge and innovation, as well as on the use of advanced technology especially in the oil and gas sector.",""],[1,"114","2","Entrepreneurial Training and Counselling Programme","RKN10 will ensure that local entrepreneurs are able to penetrate international markets through advancement in entrepreneurial training and counselling.",""],[1,"114","2","Entrepreneur Business Planning Mentorship","Emphasis will also be given to mentoring entrepreneurs in creating strategic business plans which include basic aspects of management and marketing.",""],[1,"114","5","Entrepreneurship Development Programme","The entrepreneurship development programme, therefore, is intended to enable local businesses to expand and enter the overseas market.",""],[1,"114","7","SME Development Special Fund","RKN10 has also provided a special fund for the development of small and medium enterprises (SMEs) to assist efforts to develop SMEs in this country.",""],[1,"115","3","SME Development Support","A speedier and higher level of economic growth is required to generate employment opportunities, assist the development of SMEs, as well as to increase the country's income.",""],[1,"115","1","Malay Business Leadership Training Initiative","This strategy will also encourage, and train, more Malay citizens to become industry and business leaders.",""],[1,"137","10","Small and Medium Enterprises Development Fund","Meanwhile, to support the development of small and medium enterprises, the government has allocated a total of BND100 million under the Small and Medium Enterprises Development Fund.",""],[1,"160","2","Industrial Promotion and Entrepreneurial Development Programme","Industrial Promotion and Entrepreneurial Development: Industrial and Trade Promotion Programme",""],[1,"160","2","Cooperative Development Scheme","Cooperative Development Scheme",""],[1,"137","5","SME Development Project Assessment and Endorsement Procedure","Small and Medium Enterprises development projects must be submitted to the Department of Economic Planning and Development for assessment and endorsement;",""]],"78":[[1,"107","3","Industrial Site, Broadband, and Business Incentive Support","relevant assistance will continue to be provided in the form of industrial sites, communication infrastructure including broadband, financial facilities and tax incentives to both new and existing businesses",""],[1,"107","3","Local Enterprise Applications and Products Grant Scheme","The provision of grants schemes under the Local Enterprise Applications and Products Programmes (LEAP) to new and prospective businesses by the Brunei Economic Development Board (BEDB) and the Authority for Info-Communications Technology Industry of Brunei Darussalam (AITI) represent some of the government's efforts to help local entrepreneurs strengthen their competency in businesses in order to be on par with foreign entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"107","3","Future Fund for New ICT Companies","Additional financial assistance is also provided by the government such as 'The Future Fund' for new ICT companies.",""],[1,"112","8","ICT Entrepreneurship Attraction and Business Expansion Support","BEDB through the iCentre, will further encourage local and foreign ICT entrepreneurs to set up and expand their businesses in Brunei Darussalam.",""],[1,"112","8","ICT Incubation Mentorship and Networking Programme","Furthermore, through its mentorship and networking programmes, the iCentre provides its incubatees not only with access to professional advices but also connections to potential partners and clients, both locally and internationally.",""],[1,"114","6","AITI Grant Scheme for Local ICT Companies","The AITI Grant Scheme has also been introduced to local ICT companies particularly for the development of ICT skills and software applications.",""],[1,"114","5","Local Enterprise Applications and Products (LEAP) Programme","This includes the Local Enterprise Applications and Products (LEAP) programme which provides financial assistance for the development of new products and applications that have innovative technology as well as commercial and export potential.",""],[1,"168","16","e-Business Industry Development Scheme","e-Business Industry Development Scheme",""]],"79":[[1,"107","4","Copyright and Intellectual Property Rights Protection","The protection of copyrights and intellectual property rights is the foundation towards the development of a creative and innovative economy.",""],[1,"107","5","Patent Law Enforcement for Intellectual Property Rights","a law on patent has been enforced on 1st January 2012 with the objective of strengthening intellectual property rights in the country.",""],[1,"108","2","Copyright and Intellectual Property Protection","Other than that, copyrights and intellectual property rights will be protected and respected so that foreign investments and research activities will continue to grow in the country.",""],[1,"112","7","Intellectual Property Rights Management Reform","the efficiency of the intellectual property rights (IPR) management system will be continuously enhanced by reviewing existing acts and legislations, and drafting new ones.",""],[1,"112","7","International Intellectual Property and Expertise Acquisition Strategy","An effective strategy will be formed in order to acquire intellectual property and global expertise through the international intelligent network.",""],[1,"112","7","Patent Order for Copyright Protection and Innovation Environment","The Patent Order which came into effect on 1st January 2012 is intended not only to provide copyright protection but also acts as a national policy commitment by the government in providing a conducive environment for innovation.",""]],"80":[[1,"112","6","Knowledge Infrastructure Upgrade and Broadband Expansion","To accelerate knowledge-intensive activities, the quality of knowledge info-structure networks in the country will be upgraded so that they are at par with services provided in knowledge-advanced countries.",""],[1,"113","4","Brunei Next Generation Broadband Network Project","These include providing knowledge infrastructure such as fast and advanced internet services using fiber-to-the-home (FTTH) technology through the Brunei Next Generation Broadband Network (BNBN) project.",""],[1,"126","1","National Info-Communication Infrastructure Network Development","It is the intention of the country to build a sophisticated and reliable national network of info-communication infrastructure.",""],[1,"126","2","Fiber Optic Internet Connectivity Expansion","the government will continue to improve and enhance internet connectivity in homes and business premises through the use of fibre optics technology.",""],[1,"161","5","RTB New Broadcasting Complex Phases I and II","RTB New Broadcasting Complex - Phase I and II",""],[1,"161","5","RTB New Broadcasting Complex Phase III and New Auditorium","RTB New Broadcasting Complex (Phase III) and New Auditorium",""],[1,"161","5","Digital Transmission Infrastructure","Digital Transmission Infrastructure",""]],"81":[[1,"102","1","Support for Local Products, Arts, and Handicrafts","The government will also continue to provide facilities and assistance to support the production of local products including art and handicrafts, not only for the domestic market but also internationally.",""],[1,"158","1","Poultry Industry Export Market Development","Export Market for Poultry Industry Development",""],[1,"115","2","Support for International Standards Compliance and Export Market Penetration","Efforts in producing high quality and safe products according to international standards will be continuously supported to enable these entrepreneurs to penetrate international markets.",""],[1,"115","2","Niche Product Development for Premium Halal Food","This includes producing products which have niche markets, in particular the premium halal food.",""],[1,"115","2","Private Sector Downstream Investment, R&D and Marketing Support","Similarly, private sector investments in downstream activities, R&D and marketing strategies will also be enhanced.",""],[1,"115","3","Non-Oil and Gas Industry Promotion","The government will continue to promote non-oil and gas industries and businesses",""],[1,"159","16","Primary Resource Excellence Management Incubation","Incubation and Primary Resource Excellence Management Increasing Compliance to International Standards by Local SMEs Provision of Tourism Industry Facilities",""],[1,"159","16","SME International Standards Compliance Support","Increasing Compliance to International Standards by Local SMEs",""],[1,"159","16","Tourism Industry Facilities Provision","Provision of Tourism Industry Facilities",""],[1,"160","2","Local Products Marketing Development","Mix Marketing Development for Local Products",""],[1,"160","2","Marketing Agency Development","Development of Marketing Agency",""]],"82":[[1,"124","1","High-Quality and Sustainable Infrastructure Development","the government, in collaboration with the private sector, will work together to ensure the development of high quality and sustainable infrastructure as a strategic development thrust for RKN10.",""],[1,"126","4","Green Buildings Construction Initiative","One measure that can be adopted to save the use of energy, water and other resources is by constructing green buildings.",""],[1,"126","6","Environmentally Friendly Infrastructure, Technology and Services Provision","the provision of environmentally- friendly infrastructure, technology and services.",""],[1,"126","6","Mandatory Environmental Impact Assessment for Infrastructure Projects","the requirement that the Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) is conducted in the planning stage of any infrastructure development projects.",""],[1,"128","1","Sustainable Infrastructure Provision Programme","The government will continue to provide high quality and sustainable infrastructure in the RKN10 in order to ensure that the Wawasan Brunei 2035 can be realised.",""],[1,"128","1","Public-Private Infrastructure Productivity Partnership","The government, in collaboration with the private sector and other interested parties, will make certain that the infrastructure provided can increase productivity and efficiency in the effort towards achieving a sustainable economic growth.",""],[1,"128","1","Energy Efficiency and Waste Reduction Measures","Efforts to save energy and financial resources remain a priority and these include the use of new technology that can promote efficiency and minimise waste.",""],[1,"128","1","Environmental Protection Compliance in Industrial Site Selection","Laws and regulations on environmental protection will also continue to be emphasised during the selection of new industrial sites.",""]],"83":[[1,"163","12","Air Quality Monitoring System","Monitoring of Air Quality in Brunei Darussalam including Ambience and Along the Roads",""],[1,"163","12","Landslide Rehabilitation Around Driving Circuit","Landslide Rehabilitation Around Driving Circuit",""],[1,"164","1","Danau Beach Stone Revetment Wall Construction","Construction of Stone Revetment Wall along Danau Beach",""],[1,"164","1","Pelompong Spit Coastal Protection Works Rehabilitation","Rehabilitation of Coastal Protection Works for Pelompong Spit",""],[1,"164","1","Tutong River Estuary Stabilisation Phase III","Stabilisation of Tutong River Estuary Phase III",""],[1,"164","1","Brunei Steep Slope Protection and Meragang Beach Erosion Control","Protection of Brunei Steep Slope and Control of Meragang Beach Erosion",""],[1,"164","1","Brunei River Basin Water Quality Monitoring Network","Water Quality Monitoring Network of Brunei River, Belait River, Tutong River and Temburong River",""],[1,"166","2","Study for Establishing a Hydrological Centre","Study for the Establishment of Hydrological Centre",""],[1,"158","1","Heavy Metal Pollution and Soil Erosion Survey","Survey on Heavy Metal Pollution and Soil Erosion",""]],"84":[[1,"158","4","Certification of Free From Animal Diseases Status","Certification of Free From Animal Diseases Status",""],[1,"158","4","Animal Quarantine Capacity Improvement","Improvement on Animal Quarantine Capacity/Capability - Livestock and Crops",""],[1,"158","4","Crop Quarantine Capacity Improvement","Improvement on Crop Quarantine Capability",""],[1,"159","5","Fishery Quarantine Laboratory and Research Centre Improvement","Fishery Quarantine Laboratory, Diagnostic Laboratory and Fishery Bio Technology Research Centre Improvement of Industry Productivity",""]],"85":[[1,"158","1","Marketing System Feasibility Study for Major Agricultural Commodities","Feasibility Study for the Marketing System of Major Agricultural Commodities",""],[1,"158","1","Food Development Centre Establishment Feasibility Study","Feasibility Study for the Establishment of Food Development Centre",""],[1,"168","1","Livestock and Crops Industry Regulation and Legislation Study","Study and Preparation of Regulation and Legislation Document for Livestock and Crops Industry",""]],"86":[[1,"164","7","National Street Lighting Installation Programme","Installation of Street Lighting throughout the Country",""],[1,"160","2","Gadong Market Improvement and Upgrading","Improvement and Upgrading of Gadong Market and Its Area",""]],"87":[[1,"169","1","Audio Visual Technology for Civil and Syariah Courts","Audio Visual Technology at Civil and Syariah Courts",""],[1,"169","14","e-Forensic and Cyber Surveillance System","e-Forensic and Cyber Surveillance System for Royal Brunei Police Force",""]],"88":[[1,"169","1","Road Safety Monitoring and Data Collection System","Road Safety Monitoring System and Data Collection",""]],"89":[[1,"170","5","Police Academy Construction Phase I","Construction of Police Academy - Phase I",""],[1,"170","5","Special Force Unit Building Construction","Construction of Special Force Unit Building",""],[1,"170","5","Marine Jetty and Housing Construction in Kuala Belait","Construction of Marine Jetty and Housing Kuala Belait",""],[1,"170","5","New Police Headquarters Construction in Gadong","Construction of New Police Headquarters Building, Gadong",""],[1,"170","5","Police Housing Complex Construction at Lambak Kanan","Construction of Police Housing Complex at Lambak Kanan Housing Area",""],[1,"170","5","Special Force Housing Construction at Kampong Sungai Akar","Construction of Housing for Department of Special Force at Kampong Sungai Akar",""],[1,"170","5","SPO Flat Construction at Limau Manis Police Station","Construction of SPO Flat - Limau Manis Police Station",""]]}});